<title>BELGIUM: CMB H1 1996 jumps due exceptional items.</title>
<headline>CMB H1 1996 jumps due exceptional items.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996 data</p>
<p>			 (billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			   3.65 vs     0.61</p>
<p>    Cons pre-tax exceptional gains	2.89 vs     0.06</p>
<p>    Turnover				   19.11 vs    19.70</p>
<p>    Current pre-tax profit		  0.77 vs     0.66</p>
<p>    Taxes					 0.17 vs     0.08</p>
<p>    Net profit				  3.49 vs     0.64</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian shipping group CMB NV said it made a 4.49 billion franc capital gain on the sale of its stake in Diamond Offshore Drilling Inc. It had an exceptional gain of 368 million francs on the recovery of a non-performing loan. It would write off goodwill for 2.01 billion francs.</p>
<p>The sale of the group's 20 percent stake in Bermuda-registered Pacific Basin Bulk Shipping is to be finalised in September. The group said in July the sale of the stake to Malaysian transport company Perkapalan Berhad would net it $50 million.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
